.\" Made from the kstar help (src/help.rs); do not edit. See src/manual.rs.
.TH KSTAR-UPDATE 1 "" "Kleene Star" "Kleene Star Manual"
.SH NAME
kstar\-update \- update kstar and its VS Code extension
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBkstar update\fR [options]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
On a terminal, when there is a newer release, shows a full-screen view:
this kstar's version, the latest stable and beta releases, what is new in
the chosen one, a question, then the install step by step with its output.
Left and Right choose stable or beta, Enter updates, q leaves.
.PP
Otherwise (with \-\-no-tui, \-\-check or \-\-yes, when standard input or output
is not a terminal, or with NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb) it works in plain text:
it asks GitHub for the latest stable release (through the \fBgh\fR command, or
\fBcurl\fR with GITHUB_TOKEN). If it is newer than this kstar, it shows both
versions and what the release is about, and asks "Update to vX.Y.Z?
[Y/n]". On yes it installs the release with its install script into the
folder kstar is in, which also updates the VS Code extension; on no it
changes nothing. Betas (pre-releases such as 0.2.5-beta) are offered only
with \-\-beta, or on the beta channel of the full-screen view.
.PP
When standard input is not a terminal (a script or CI), it does not ask and
does not update: pass \-\-yes.
.PP
If VS Code is installed (the \fBcode\fR command) and kstar is up to date, it
also makes sure the Kleene Star extension matches this kstar: when it is
missing or from another release, it downloads kleene-star-<version>.vsix
from this kstar's release, checks its SHA-256 checksum and installs it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fR
only say whether a newer release exists, and whether the VS Code extension matches, without installing anything
.TP
\fB\-\-beta\fR
also offer betas: update to the latest pre-release when it is newer than the latest stable release
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
update without asking
.TP
\fB\-\-no-vscode\fR
leave VS Code alone (so does KSTAR_NO_VSCODE=1)
.TP
\fB\-\-no-tui\fR
plain text and a [Y/n] question instead of the full-screen view
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\fR \fI<name>\fR
the colours of the screen: auto (the default: the terminal's own colours), light, dark or high-contrast. KSTAR_THEME and the config file work as for \fBkstar run\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBkstar update \-\-check\fR
see whether there is a newer release
.TP
\fBkstar update\fR
update, after asking
.TP
\fBkstar update \-\-beta \-\-yes\fR
update to the newest release, betas included, without asking
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBkstar\fR(1),
\fBkstar\-help\fR(1)
.PP
The reference and the tutorial: https://github.com/Pratham71/kleene\-star
